00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200 align:start position:0%
<v Mara>Welcome back to Harbor Voices, the show about small ports and the people who keep them.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.800
<v Mara>Today we are at the Grey Point lighthouse with its keeper, Tobias Renn.

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:15.500
<v Tobias>Thanks, Mara. The lamp here still burns colza oil, about fourteen litres a night in winter.

4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Tobias>People assume it went electric decades ago, but the harbor board voted to keep the old burner in 1987.

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
[MUSIC]

6
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
<v Mara>This episode is brought to you by Saltline Rope. Use the code HARBOR for ten percent off at saltline.com.

7
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.400
<v Mara>Tobias, you keep a ledger of every ship that passes. How far back does it go?

8
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:46.900
<v Tobias>The first entry is from March 1902, a coal barge called the <i>Wren</i>. We have 212 volumes now, and I add a page most nights.

9
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:11.000
<v Tobias>The strangest entry is a fishing boat that signalled with a kitchen mirror because its radio had drowned.

10
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:18.300
<v Mara>And the board wants to scan the whole ledger by next spring, which will take two volunteers about nine months.

11
00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:23.000
<v Tobias>That is the plan. I will believe it when the scanner arrives.
